Exact held-state head `19dae14d5cc71d3859938ffe218230d542f7498f` is CI-green (run 30483872955: check, fuzz, hygiene all passed) and received two fresh session reviews with no actionable findings.

The fresh review cycle addressed:

- approval-history API drift (`submitted_at` does not exist), with first-attempt/unambiguous receipt semantics;
- stale/closed/shared-head request refusal before protected approval;
- claim/outcome TOCTOU under one anchored-state lock;
- exit 3 contract refusals vs exit 4 operational failures;
- result JSON Schema/Go validation drift;
- Gate App authority on nested/non-main branches;
- and, most importantly, the unsafe generic-Actions `gate-state` writer.

The last issue is contained, not hand-waved: the executor job is statically false, its token is read-only, the plan is `blocked_security_decision` with no `gate-state` writer, and the operator runbook contains no activation steps. PR remains draft.

Operator security decision still required before more implementation: authorize or reject the proposed one-App process-custodied ordering (post-approval token creation → claim CAS/refetch → exact merge → result CAS) plus no-merge-token expired-claim reconciliation. No App/config/ruleset/grant/bootstrap/canary/merge action was performed.

